00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:41.122
(swooshing sound)

00:11:41.122 --> 00:11:42.139
(bang)

00:11:42.139 --> 00:11:44.972
(swooshing sound)

00:11:45.882 --> 00:11:47.949
- How can you make that all important

00:11:47.949 --> 00:11:50.275
first impression count to set the tone

00:11:50.275 --> 00:11:52.041
for the relationship that follows

00:11:52.041 --> 00:11:56.468
and the potential business
that can result from it.

00:11:56.468 --> 00:11:58.185
My advice would be to tell them a story.

00:11:58.185 --> 00:11:59.650
It doesn't have to be War and Peace,

00:11:59.650 --> 00:12:00.973
and it shouldn't be.

00:12:00.973 --> 00:12:03.331
But stories spark interest,
keep people engaged

00:12:03.331 --> 00:12:05.450
and help them to understand.

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:08.042
Stories allow the conscious mind to relax.

00:12:08.042 --> 00:12:10.694
But at the same time
the pattern perceiving,

00:12:10.694 --> 00:12:12.677
unconscious mind can make the match

00:12:12.677 --> 00:12:15.592
and use the story to help
them connect with you.

00:12:15.592 --> 00:12:17.504
Too often in business we try and connect

00:12:17.504 --> 00:12:19.893
with people on a rational level.

00:12:19.893 --> 00:12:21.472
But this isn't enough to inspire

00:12:21.472 --> 00:12:25.878
and influence them to take
action for your cause.

00:12:25.878 --> 00:12:28.362
Let me break it down into the three ways

00:12:28.362 --> 00:12:30.060
people tend to answer the question

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:32.905
and give you some examples.

00:12:32.905 --> 00:12:35.255
The first answer that most people

00:12:35.255 --> 00:12:37.130
give is the standard answer.

00:12:37.130 --> 00:12:38.034
That you will have heard,

00:12:38.034 --> 00:12:40.462
I may well have said, many times.

00:12:40.462 --> 00:12:41.395
What do you do?

00:12:41.395 --> 00:12:43.364
I'm an accountant.

00:12:43.364 --> 00:12:45.492
Whether or not people actually understand

00:12:45.492 --> 00:12:48.541
what you do they think
they know what you do.

00:12:48.541 --> 00:12:50.033
And so they switch off.

00:12:50.033 --> 00:12:51.411
They've met loads of accountants

00:12:51.411 --> 00:12:53.997
who have all given the same answer.

00:12:53.997 --> 00:12:56.136
They very rarely follow
up with a question.

00:12:56.136 --> 00:12:58.558
And if they do it's often out of pity

00:12:58.558 --> 00:13:00.904
rather than genuine curiosity.

00:13:00.904 --> 00:13:02.635
And I'm picking on accountants here,

00:13:02.635 --> 00:13:05.105
but it's the same if
you answer's solicitor,

00:13:05.105 --> 00:13:07.514
web developer, florist or magician.

00:13:07.514 --> 00:13:09.588
People have a good idea of what you do

00:13:09.588 --> 00:13:11.755
and no connection is made.

00:13:12.705 --> 00:13:16.225
So it's the next thing you
can do to grab their attention

00:13:16.225 --> 00:13:19.448
and create some curiosity in them.

00:13:19.448 --> 00:13:22.737
You could reply, I help people
save money on their taxes,

00:13:22.737 --> 00:13:25.013
or I take the hassle away from people

00:13:25.013 --> 00:13:28.000
when it comes to their business finances.

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:29.587
That's certainly a better answer

00:13:29.587 --> 00:13:33.104
than the first response
of I'm an accountant.

00:13:33.104 --> 00:13:35.034
And it shows them that
you can solve a problem

00:13:35.034 --> 00:13:37.279
that many businesses face.

00:13:37.279 --> 00:13:41.232
It also creates a little bit
of curiosity, but barely.

00:13:41.232 --> 00:13:42.469
If you wish to answer like this

00:13:42.469 --> 00:13:45.041
try and make your answer
a little more memorable.

00:13:45.041 --> 00:13:46.870
Try and inject some humor to make

00:13:46.870 --> 00:13:49.029
your great first impression.

00:13:49.029 --> 00:13:50.868
A friend of mine introduces himself

00:13:50.868 --> 00:13:53.289
as a crime fighting space man.

00:13:53.289 --> 00:13:55.105
It gets a laugh every time and always

00:13:55.105 --> 00:13:57.329
invites the question well
what do you mean by that?

00:13:57.329 --> 00:13:58.885
This gives him the opportunity to talk

00:13:58.885 --> 00:14:01.185
a little bit about his
architectural practice

00:14:01.185 --> 00:14:02.907
where he redesigns buildings

00:14:02.907 --> 00:14:06.355
that are regularly the
victim of break-ins.

00:14:06.355 --> 00:14:09.746
It's a great introduction
and is sure to be remembered.

00:14:09.746 --> 00:14:11.410
But it's not enough to make that lasting

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:14.867
connection on a subconscious level.

00:14:14.867 --> 00:14:17.907
So, here's the third way, and the best way

00:14:17.907 --> 00:14:20.374
to answer the question what do you do?

00:14:20.374 --> 00:14:22.041
Incorporate a story.

00:14:22.878 --> 00:14:26.966
A friend of mine, whenever
he is asked this question,

00:14:26.966 --> 00:14:28.355
tells this story,

00:14:28.355 --> 00:14:32.231
growing up, both of his parents
owned their own businesses,

00:14:32.231 --> 00:14:35.312
and were never in control
of their finances.

00:14:35.312 --> 00:14:36.736
This meant that every January

00:14:36.736 --> 00:14:39.001
there would be panic in his house

00:14:39.001 --> 00:14:41.107
and many nasty surprises that resulted

00:14:41.107 --> 00:14:45.286
in a lot of unpleasantness,
arguments, and canceled plans.

00:14:45.286 --> 00:14:48.304
Because of this he's
grown up hating surprises,

00:14:48.304 --> 00:14:50.237
and has dedicated his life to ensuring

00:14:50.237 --> 00:14:52.240
that other business owners never get

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:55.588
nasty surprises when it
comes to their finances.

00:14:55.588 --> 00:14:56.756
So what does he do?

00:14:56.756 --> 00:14:58.271
He's an accountant.

00:14:58.271 --> 00:14:59.585
Now imagine you're networking

00:14:59.585 --> 00:15:01.811
and you've heard the
answer I'm an accountant

00:15:01.811 --> 00:15:05.487
seven or eight times and
then you hear this story.

00:15:05.487 --> 00:15:08.546
Which accountant are you
going to pass your work to?

00:15:08.546 --> 00:15:09.459
That's right.

00:15:09.459 --> 00:15:11.455
The one that hates surprises.

00:15:11.455 --> 00:15:12.910
He's made a connection with you,

00:15:12.910 --> 00:15:15.139
and you'll also find it easy to refer

00:15:15.139 --> 00:15:18.056
to friends and business associates.

00:15:18.972 --> 00:15:22.067
Notice that step two invites a question

00:15:22.067 --> 00:15:23.927
to which the answer is step one.

00:15:23.927 --> 00:15:27.109
And that step three includes
step two and step one.

00:15:27.109 --> 00:15:29.241
It's important to include all three steps

00:15:29.241 --> 00:15:30.856
but it must be done in this order

00:15:30.856 --> 00:15:33.526
to grab the attention, generate curiosity,

00:15:33.526 --> 00:15:36.198
keep them hooked and make the connection.

00:15:36.198 --> 00:15:37.853
- Number two is body language.

00:15:37.853 --> 00:15:40.252
How you walk, how you stand, alright.

00:15:40.252 --> 00:15:41.945
Are you in an open posture,

00:15:41.945 --> 00:15:44.130
or are you arms crossed
and lookin' pissed?

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:46.138
Guys the way that you carry yourself

00:15:46.138 --> 00:15:48.237
and the non verbal
communication that you're doing

00:15:48.237 --> 00:15:50.600
with your body is critical and essential

00:15:50.600 --> 00:15:52.061
to that first impression.

00:15:52.061 --> 00:15:54.092
Eye contact, smile, handshake,

00:15:54.092 --> 00:15:55.879
all these things play a factor.

00:15:55.879 --> 00:15:58.021
And if you're fallin' down or lacking

00:15:58.021 --> 00:16:00.509
in one of these areas
it's going to reek havoc

00:16:00.509 --> 00:16:03.181
on those first impressions, all of 'em.

00:16:03.181 --> 00:16:04.675
- Fake it, til you make it,

00:16:04.675 --> 00:16:06.474
is often misinterpreted and it's a great

00:16:06.474 --> 00:16:08.129
piece of advice, don't get me wrong.

00:16:08.129 --> 00:16:10.965
But fake it til you make it applies only

00:16:10.965 --> 00:16:13.675
to body language and non
verbal communication.

00:16:13.675 --> 00:16:15.396
When you start using
fake it til you make it

00:16:15.396 --> 00:16:16.936
in the things that you say,

00:16:16.936 --> 00:16:18.274
that's when you run into trouble.

00:16:18.274 --> 00:16:21.288
So for instance, the CEO,
who had a terrible quarter

00:16:21.288 --> 00:16:22.499
speaking in front of his company

00:16:22.499 --> 00:16:23.866
gets up there and says, hey guys,

00:16:23.866 --> 00:16:26.013
we're doing great, you know, not exactly

00:16:26.013 --> 00:16:27.913
where we want, but this is really on track

00:16:27.913 --> 00:16:29.526
and we, our numbers were kind of off

00:16:29.526 --> 00:16:31.646
in the projections, so
we're killin' it right now.

00:16:31.646 --> 00:16:33.738
Or right, guy at a networking event

00:16:33.738 --> 00:16:35.316
who goes off and pretends that he has

00:16:35.316 --> 00:16:36.419
a kind of status at his company

00:16:36.419 --> 00:16:37.508
that he can hook people up,

00:16:37.508 --> 00:16:39.191
he goes, you know, I'm in,
just send me your resume

00:16:39.191 --> 00:16:40.721
I'll get you a job no problem.

00:16:40.721 --> 00:16:42.419
And he's got no such power.

00:16:42.419 --> 00:16:43.486
This happens all the time.

00:16:43.486 --> 00:16:45.748
People fake power that they don't have.

00:16:45.748 --> 00:16:47.609
Or a guy who wants to impress a girl

00:16:47.609 --> 00:16:49.608
takes her to a nice
restaurant, really great.

00:16:49.608 --> 00:16:51.904
But rather than acting like, you know,

00:16:51.904 --> 00:16:52.942
this is a special occasion,

00:16:52.942 --> 00:16:54.980
pretends this is something
he does all the time.

00:16:54.980 --> 00:16:57.295
That kind of stuff does not fly.

00:16:57.295 --> 00:16:58.675
So here's what you want to do.

00:16:58.675 --> 00:17:00.754
Fake it til you make it
in the way that you speak

00:17:00.754 --> 00:17:01.899
and the way that you carry yourself,

00:17:01.899 --> 00:17:03.618
your tonality, the way
that you gesticulate,

00:17:03.618 --> 00:17:05.891
the way that you breathe, that's
going to affect your head,

00:17:05.891 --> 00:17:08.612
which is going to actually
change the way that you feel.

00:17:08.612 --> 00:17:10.837
Right, your physiology
does change your emotion.

00:17:10.837 --> 00:17:12.165
And we've talked about this at length,

00:17:12.165 --> 00:17:14.245
I don't want to go into it here but,

00:17:14.245 --> 00:17:16.348
when it comes to the
things that are coming out

00:17:16.348 --> 00:17:19.194
of your mouth be honest to a fault.

00:17:19.194 --> 00:17:20.446
So for instance, that CEO,

00:17:20.446 --> 00:17:22.612
might get up there and say, guys, listen,

00:17:22.612 --> 00:17:24.579
this quarter was a disappointment.

00:17:24.579 --> 00:17:26.353
We did not hit our numbers,

00:17:26.353 --> 00:17:27.932
we didn't do the things
that we needed to do.

00:17:27.932 --> 00:17:28.925
I've spoken to many of you,

00:17:28.925 --> 00:17:30.411
I've reflected on what needs to happen

00:17:30.411 --> 00:17:33.275
and here's how we're going
to do it going forward.

00:17:33.275 --> 00:17:35.371
The confidence that he
speaks with is what's going

00:17:35.371 --> 00:17:37.111
to inspire people to hang on, to continue.

00:17:37.111 --> 00:17:39.910
And the honesty's going
to make them trust him,

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:41.994
that holy cow, we can do this,

00:17:41.994 --> 00:17:43.733
he's not just going to
sugar coat everything.

00:17:43.733 --> 00:17:46.607
Take the guy who takes a
woman to a nice restaurant,

00:17:46.607 --> 00:17:48.418
right, rather than like going
in and being like oh yeah.

00:17:48.418 --> 00:17:50.154
Pretending he knows the maitre'D,

00:17:50.154 --> 00:17:51.382
or that this happens all the time,

00:17:51.382 --> 00:17:53.122
or talking about his investment portfolio,

00:17:53.122 --> 00:17:54.719
or whatever it is, he
might go in there and say,

00:17:54.719 --> 00:17:55.942
listen I got to be honest,

00:17:55.942 --> 00:17:58.597
this place is way nicer
than the restaurants

00:17:58.597 --> 00:18:00.731
I normally go to, so I hope that

00:18:00.731 --> 00:18:01.704
you're impressed by the food,

00:18:01.704 --> 00:18:04.258
and that makes you laugh
extra hard at my jokes.

00:18:04.258 --> 00:18:06.029
Right, play off fun, funny.

00:18:06.029 --> 00:18:08.007
But you can let people
know this is special.

00:18:08.007 --> 00:18:08.840
This is nice.

00:18:08.840 --> 00:18:11.097
That honesty is going to let her her know,

00:18:11.097 --> 00:18:12.754
which is a huge concern
for women by the way

00:18:12.754 --> 00:18:13.775
that they men that they're dating

00:18:13.775 --> 00:18:16.031
are not being real, are not being honest.

00:18:16.031 --> 00:18:19.360
when you show things that
might not be to your favor,

00:18:19.360 --> 00:18:22.298
right, and you're not doing
it in a calculated way.

00:18:22.298 --> 00:18:23.809
but you're doing it because it's honest.

00:18:23.809 --> 00:18:26.337
that's going to create, create
a bond of trust between you

00:18:26.337 --> 00:18:27.772
that is actually going
to make the relationship

00:18:27.772 --> 00:18:29.452
go much, much better.

00:18:29.452 --> 00:18:30.351
(swooshing sound)

